ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T16:21:03-07:00","id":1488900,"title":"","content":"Never thought I'd see the day.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer Revised was sort of my bridge between Vampire: The Masquerade and Mage: The Ascension. So the book, for all its faults, has a special place in my heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T21:33:01-07:00","id":1488935,"title":"","content":"Doesn't seem to be out yet. Does anyone know how much it will cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T23:13:56-07:00","id":1488942,"title":"","content":"Of course not. I'm not expecting it to be released until middle or late afternoon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T23:33:34-07:00","id":1488943,"title":"","content":"I've always liked mixing Sorcerers in with the Mages in the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T06:50:45-07:00","id":1488965,"title":"","content":"I'm thrilling for M20 Sorcerer coming out today! Can't wait to put my hands (or mouse cursor hahahaha) on it! Sorcerer is one of my favourite books and I simply adore its Revised edition (and the book cover is mesmerizing).<br /> I know they said it's gonna have more details about Twilight Project and Arcanum, but I hope to see other Societies descripted in previous books. Maison Liban is my favourite and I'm going to even using them in my future DA20 Werewolf game (I'm planning as well using them in V5 game). <br /> I'm currently playing as a sorcerer Kinfolk in my friend's WtA game and even if Sorcerer Revised can be used in 20th Anniversary editions, I wanted to try using only things released already in 20th ed. He has Alchemy and in the future I'm purchasing Psychometry, Teleknesis and Empathetic Healing (all from V20 HH II and Kinfolk 20). I was planning making my character go after Soul Stealing since 20th Ed didn't have Psychic Vampirism, but having these good news about finally releasing M20 Sorcerer makes me hopeful to see this awesome power back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2511-broskandar","name":"Broskandar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T07:13:13-07:00","id":1488970,"title":"","content":"If it's what I suspect it is (an official version of the <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b> Storyteller's Vault product), then its set of societies is <i>comprehensive</i>, and even includes some pre-existing sorcery societies that I didn't even know existed.<br /> <br /> Ditto with its set of Numina: <b>S:PoP</b> covers even <i>more</i> ground than <b>S:Rev</b>. This includes Paths practiced by some of those societies I just mentioned, a <i>full</i> spread of Psychic Phenomena, True Faith, and even Infernal Investments and Paths. <br /> <br /> Frankly, if the new <b>S20</b> <i>isn't</i> an official version of <b>S:PoP</b>, I suspect I'll be disappointed: it sets a high bar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-03-2022, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T07:30:28-07:00","id":1488973,"title":"","content":"Yes. Paths of Power did a good job. I have some criticisms that made me not use it on my friend's game, but it doesn't take away the merit and dedication of the writer behind it. Also, Revised was already compatible anyway with 20th Ed, so I wouldn't mind if M20 Sorcerer would be just an update of simple rules (like powers in V20 HH II and Kinfolk 20 were).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2511-broskandar","name":"Broskandar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T07:59:24-07:00","id":1488975,"title":"","content":"Not to derail the topic; what are your criticisms of Paths of Power? I'd like to know what you're hoping that M20 Sorcerer does differently than it. (I have my own list of concerns; but I'm hoping to hear your take on it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T09:31:23-07:00","id":1488979,"title":"","content":"Actually, I would welcome some comparisons between PoP and S20 here. I have neither and currently have two players on Revised rules, so I'm curious how they measure up.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm hoping for a more interchangeable psychic powers and sorcery paths, and make the distinction a mechanical one in application instead of 'classes'. Some more rituals and maybe a go at a light resonance system would also be cool. Also, streamlined aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T09:51:27-07:00","id":1488981,"title":"","content":"Can one of you guys who buys it first post on here and let me know if Sorcerer 20 is just an official version of Paths of Power? I already own PoP and I don\u2019t wanna buy the same thing twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T10:03:55-07:00","id":1488984,"title":"","content":"Even if S20 turns out to be based on S:PoP, I think the more appropriate way of viewing it would be as a new edition. I do not doubt that there will be differences. <br /> <br /> But yeah; if I manage to get my hands on it (big \u201cif\u201d right now, due to shaky finances), I'll let you know how they compare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T12:49:40-07:00","id":1488999,"title":"","content":"First impressions (comparing to Revised):<br /> - Tweaks to Path caps and Attribute + Ability choice for making it more coherent with style and paradigm. Ok.<br /> - General Aspect lists for Paths. Good. &quot;Metaphysical Weight&quot; is a clever way to cover multiple things at once, I like that.<br /> - Rituals are a bit more flexible. Essentially, trade casting time for stronger or specialized effect. Good.<br /> - Mini-Consensus check with a Witnesses chart that counters vulgar effects in public. Onlookers soak successes. Not too bad.<br /> - Not going into the detail of individual Paths yet. No 6 dots, which is ok with me. Annoyingly, after establishing the general Aspect lists, Paths still get their own lists. Missed the mark here.<br /> - Some proper Necromancy, separate from Spirits and other Ephemera. Overdue.<br /> - Technomancy is Necrotechnomancy, which is funny, but a simple Technomancy Path would have sufficed. I'll probably continue to use my Homebrew.<br /> - List of Psychic Phenomena and Sorcery Paths has a few new additions. I had expected a wee bit more, but space is limited, I get that.<br /> - There are some dupes between the two, or at least very similar powers that could have simply been the same thing. As I said in my previous post, making the Paths open for both and then have a distinctive difference in casting would have been more economic. Oh well.<br /> - More societies and affiliations. Reads fine at first glance, but I need to take more time.<br /> <br /> So far fluff and crunch look fine. The artwork is really nice. Spotted some minor editing mistakes, but nothing glaring (yet).<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot to mention- no index : (","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-03-2022, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T13:01:04-07:00","id":1489003,"title":"","content":"Ah, I imagined they wouldn't put the 6th-Dot powers in Sorcerer20, which is a shame. But ok. Revised edition is already good for 20th Ed.<br /> Separating Summoning/Warding/Binding between entities feels more work and more XP sink. Doesn't feel optimized.<br /> The other things you reported feels OK.<br /> Still need to get the book and give my own review.<br /> Thank you for your input!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2511-broskandar","name":"Broskandar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T13:20:23-07:00","id":1489004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broskandar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489003#post1489003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separating Summoning/Warding/Binding between entities feels more work and more XP sink. Doesn't feel optimized.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be precise, both Ephemera and S/W/B still exist as separate Paths. Ephemera is more geared towards classic Mediums, S/W/B must be learned separately for each creature type. Necromancy now exists as a specialized Path for Ghosts (it doesn't say Wraith, but uses WtO terms in the description of effects).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T14:00:35-07:00","id":1489011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broskandar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489003#post1489003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I imagined they wouldn't put the 6th-Dot powers in Sorcerer20, which is a shame. But ok. Revised edition is already good for 20th Ed.<br /> Separating Summoning/Warding/Binding between entities feels more work and more XP sink. Doesn't feel optimized.<br /> The other things you reported feels OK.<br /> Still need to get the book and give my own review.<br /> Thank you for your input!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m strongly on team \u201cbeing a necromancer should not give you equal skills in the summoning and command of faeries\u201d on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T15:28:17-07:00","id":1489019,"title":"","content":"Does it address M20's Focus system (Paradigm, Practice, Instruments)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T16:02:51-07:00","id":1489022,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> when a sorcerer begins learning a path, they must choose a practice to determine how they go about casting the spell/ritual(page12) and it calls out the practice sections of M20 and Book of Secrets. However it doesn't waste time expl","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T16:52:17-07:00","id":1489031,"title":"","content":"Ok, nice. The Witness rules are clear and simple and address why (even apart from Technocrats breaking down their door) Sorcerers don\u2019t generally defy the consensus in public despite not having paradox to worry about. Good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T17:27:28-07:00","id":1489034,"title":"","content":"Finally got at my computer! I'm checking the sample pages and I'm seeing Starlight in the list, a Hedge Magic which uses Humanity presented in Ghost Hunters. <br /> <br /> Question: Does the powers in Revised translated to 20th Ed also need now to use Humanity? In Revised, we didn't need to worry about Humanity. I'm worried that Revised Paths now need to use it (since I'm playing as a Kinfolk, I don't use).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2511-broskandar","name":"Broskandar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T20:37:58-07:00","id":1489053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1488979#post1488979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I would welcome some comparisons between PoP and S20 here. I have neither and currently have two players on Revised rules, so I'm curious how they measure up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay; I have S20. I haven't been able to take a deep dive into it yet; but already I can tell you this: it's <i>not</i> based on S:PoP. <br /> <br /> Moreover, I am glad I bought S:PoP. Of the two, S:PoP is the more comprehensive. I suspect that what I'm going to do will be to use S:PoP as the default for sorcerers in my chronicles, but will look through S20 for areas that it does better and incorporate them. <br /> <br /> I'll give you a more in-depth report once I've studied the issue more closely.<br /> <br /> First thing I'll note: Charles Siegel, the author of S:PoP, is <i>one of</i> the authors of S20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-03-2022, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T01:12:44-07:00","id":1489067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broskandar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489034#post1489034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally got at my computer! I'm checking the sample pages and I'm seeing Starlight in the list, a Hedge Magic which uses Humanity presented in Ghost Hunters.<br /> <br /> Question: Does the powers in Revised translated to 20th Ed also need now to use Humanity? In Revised, we didn't need to worry about Humanity. I'm worried that Revised Paths now need to use it (since I'm playing as a Kinfolk, I don't use).</div> </div> </div> </div>The book does not use capital H Humanity as a mechanic anywhere. Starlight depends somewhat on Willpower- I don't have Ghost Hunters to compare, but I suspect Humanity was used there to make it compatible with Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489053#post1489053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll give you a more in-depth report once I've studied the issue more closely.<br /> <br /> First thing I'll note: Charles Siegel, the author of S:PoP, is <i>one of</i> the authors of S20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T05:00:31-07:00","id":1489093,"title":"","content":"On closer examination: <br /> <br /> I'm doing a 3-way comparison between SRev, S:PoP, and S20. First thing I notice is the page counts: SRev has 133 pages; S:PoP has 167 pages; S20 has 113 pages. Yep; S20 has <i>fewer</i> pages than SRev. <br /> <br /> S20's Aspects seem a little\u2026 problematic: as I read it, the more Aspects a Path has the more successes you need to achieve in order to do anything: \u201cWhen the hedge magician casts a spell, they must choose what level of each Aspect they want to include, with the default being zero \u2014 and therefore, no effect \u2014 in each.\u201d \u2026 \u201cWhen the spell is cast, it requires one success for each rank in each Aspect, plus a single success for the spell as a whole.\u201d<br /> <br /> To illustrate my concern, take a look at Conjuration: <br /> <br /> \u201c<b>Aspects:</b> Conjuration uses Aspects of Distance, Number of Targets, and Weight.\u201d So in order to cast the simplest Conjuration spell, you need four successes: one for the spell, one for a Distance of only a few feet, one for a single target, and one for a Weight of less than an ounce. <br /> <br /> By contrast, SRev has a single success give you one level in every relevant Aspect, with additional successes only needed for <i>additional</i> levels <i>after</i> the first. So a single success in Conjuration lets you Conjure one item weighing less than an ounce over no more than a couple of feet. Same effect; but one success vs. four successes. Oops\u2026<br /> <br /> S:PoP is similar to S20 in this regard: you need one success per level of Aspect per Aspect. <br /> <br /> Unless I'm misreading something? <br /> <br /> The simplest solution in S20 is to say that the single success needed for the spell itself gives you the first level in all relevant Aspects automatically; additional successes are used to raise Aspects to higher levels. <br /> <br /> How do I submit errata?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T05:22:07-07:00","id":1489097,"title":"","content":"SRev handles Witnesses in a binary fashion: if there are any Witnesses, the spell fails. In S:PoP, Witnesses impose a difficulty increase, up to +3. In S20, Witnesses remove successes, up to 5 for large crowds. <br /> <br /> SRev and S:PoP assume that magicians have an optional fuel (\u201cMana\u201d) that's different from Quintessence; S20 flat-out makes sorcerers use the same Quintessence that mages use: it even renames the Path of Mana Manipulation to Quintessence Manipulation. Speaking of Mana/Quintessence, SRev has a Background called Mana; S:PoP has an equivalent Background called Techn\u00ea. S20 doesn't have either; but I'm assuming you can achieve the same result by taking the Avatar Background (with the caveat that a magician's Avatar is still Sleeping, and isn't going to be giving him any guidance). That said, that's speculation on my part; S20 simply doesn't address the issue. <br /> <br /> And on the subject of Backgrounds: SRev has Chol\u00e9, Guide, Mana, and Status; S:PoP has Guide, Spirit Ridden, and Techn\u00ea; S20 has Artifact. As well, S20 says \u201cBackgrounds presented in <b>Mage 20</b> p. 301-328 can work for most sorcerers, but several only apply to mages.\u201d It doesn't go into any more detail than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T05:53:20-07:00","id":1489099,"title":"","content":"Paths: both S:PoP and S20 have all of the Paths found in SRev (though the latter renames Mana Manipulation as Quintessence Manipulation and Shadowcasting as Shadows); so I'll focus on what new Paths each introduces. <br /> <br /> S:PoP gives us Chronomancy, Mediumship, Saturnal Anima, Saturnal Manes, Scrying, Spirit Awakening, and Spirit Chasing. Saturnal Anima/Manes effectively come packaged with the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon, a sorcerous society lifted from W20's Wyld West supplement. Spirit Awakening and Spirit Chasing originated in\u2026 I want to say the Revised Dreamspeakers Tradition Book? Mediumship is a new name for Ephemera, a Path that made appearances in the Year of the Hunter books but somehow didn't make it into SRev. <br /> <br /> S20 gives us Ephemera, Illusion, Maelstroms, Mortal Necromancy, Necronics, and Starlight. The last four of these originated in Ghost Hunters, I think. I definitely applaud the inclusion of Ephemera and Illusion; but I think I would have preferred Chronomancy and Scrying rather than the Ghost Hunters Paths. <br /> <br /> SRev presents specific Attribute+Ability pools for each Path; S:PoP requires you to decide on a Focus for your sorcerer; for each Path, the Attribute comes from the Path and the Ability is to be chosen from one of those associated with your Practice. In S20, the Attribute comes from you Affiliation and the Ability comes from your Practice. <br /> <br /> The upside of this is that S:PoP and S20 have much more flexibility in establishing your own dice pool for your Paths; but they lose some of the ease of use that SRev's established pools provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T06:40:58-07:00","id":1489105,"title":"","content":"Psychic Phenomena: S:PoP adds Empathic Healing, but it's otherwise the same as SRev. S20 adds Shadow, but it's otherwise the same as SRev. The big difference is how you use them: SRev gives you Attribute+Ability pools for the Psychic Phenomena; S:PoP and S20 make you spend a point of Willpower and roll your Willpower pool. I'm off two minds about this: on the one hand, Willpower can be very hard to come by; forcing psychics to spend it to use their powers severely limits their powers. On the other hand, SRev's Psychic Phenomena didn't have any drawbacks compared to its Paths, which required the magician to use what M20 calls Practices and Instruments. A possible compromise might be to say that Psychic Phenomena require an expenditure of 1 Willpower per scene: that is, spend one Willpower, and you can use any of your Psychic Phenomena for the rest of the scene. <br /> <br /> SRev and S20 cover Paths and Psychic Phenomena; S:PoP also covers True Faith and Investments and Dark Paths. S20 presumably skips the former because M20 already had it covered, and the latter because Book of the Fallen covers it. By contrast, S:PoP builds on both: it adds a few features to True Faith, and it adds some Dark Paths for infernalism. <br /> <br /> One final thing that S:PoP and S20 have in common: both allow mages to create Paths, adapting the rules for creating Talismans from Book of Secrets to do so. S20 calls this out as something the Technocracy specializes in: by creating a Path out of what would normally be a Vulgar Effect and teaching it to Extraordinary Citizens, they can push an Effect to be Coincidental, and then Mundane. <br /> <br /> While I like this in principle, I have concerns about putting it into practice. In particular, I don't think that Talisman creation is the most appropriate way of modeling this. I'd prefer that the Terranorming rules from Operative's Dossier be used instead, or perhaps in conjunction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T07:57:42-07:00","id":1489112,"title":"","content":"And my final word on the subject: S20 is basically a stripped down version of S:PoP. If you have the latter, you probably don't need the former. There are a few minor differences between the two (most notably the way Witnesses are handled, and how S20 bases a Path's Attribute off of your Affiliation); but that's about it. The only reason I'd recommend S20 over S:PoP is that the former is officially endorsed, whereas S:PoP contains some material that (while nice) <i>isn't</i> officially sanctioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T08:51:09-07:00","id":1489113,"title":"","content":"Hm, coming from Revised.. I like most of the rule tweaks in S20 (except for Aspects) and will probably just switch to them (except for Aspects). I may get PoP just out of curiosity, but don't feel it would be strictly necessary.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, it's a 20th Anniversary product and as such it should be a round-up of oWoD material on the theme, with some cleaned up rules. It does that. If they ever do a 5e version though, it needs some beefier changes.<br /> <br /> Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> for the synopsis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T11:20:43-07:00","id":1489137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489112#post1489112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my final word on the subject: S20 is basically a stripped down version of S:PoP. If you have the latter, you probably don't need the former. There are a few minor differences between the two (most notably the way Witnesses are handled, and how S20 bases a Path's Attribute off of your Affiliation); but that's about it. The only reason I'd recommend S20 over S:PoP is that the former is officially endorsed, whereas S:PoP contains some material that (while nice) <i>isn't</i> officially sanctioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I ended up buying S20 for the endorsement and was really impressed, especially with the section on Affiliations, which differs from PoP in a few ways (in particular the sections on the Star Council and the Thal\u2019hun as well as the Norse sorcerers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 08-04-2022, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T11:44:26-07:00","id":1489139,"title":"","content":"Yeah; it seems that they've replaced wannabe Norse sorcerers with the genuine article. Up to and including a different name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T13:39:09-07:00","id":1489147,"title":"","content":"Well I bought it. At some future date I'll get all three PDFs printed up, collated, and then pick and choose what works from these and the older editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T17:43:31-07:00","id":1489173,"title":"","content":"So to be different from the others here - I had already bought M20 Sorcerer but reading this post had me go out and buy Sorcerer Paths of Power. lol<br /> <br /> Also the review was interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T03:25:08-07:00","id":1489212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489093#post1489093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S20's Aspects seem a little\u2026 problematic: as I read it, the more Aspects a Path has the more successes you need to achieve in order to do anything: \u201cWhen the hedge magician casts a spell, they must choose what level of each Aspect they want to include, with the default being zero \u2014 and therefore, no effect \u2014 in each.\u201d \u2026 \u201cWhen the spell is cast, it requires one success for each rank in each Aspect, plus a single success for the spell as a whole.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>What's more, Effects that were previously unlocked with Path level are now handled as Aspect, too. This completely breaks with RAW where the Path descriptions have just been copypasted.<br /> <br /> Example Shapeshifting:<br /> To make cosmetic changes (Scale \u2022) to themselves (Subject \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) with a single animal feature (Disparity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) would require 10 successes. Obviously it is intended that Subject and Disparity are meant as total success level required, but due to the rule change it just doesn't parse like that. Sloppy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T08:29:48-07:00","id":1489230,"title":"","content":"Like I said: how do I submit errata? It's an advance release specifically so that errata can be submitted; but I don't know how to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T08:49:31-07:00","id":1489231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class