"title":"","content":"I am not a fan of the thing of where they at the start of the Hedge Magic section said &quot;each path will have example rituals&quot; then suddenly turn around and not have them on the Paths like Starlight and Weather Control...I don't get the rationale for why Weather Control doesn't use rituals at all.<br /> <br /> The other thing I wonder is if Enchantment requires you to buy each individual enchantment as a ritual in addition to buying the path levels...because considering how resource-intensive and time intensive the path is...making it a huge xp sink seems very counterintuitive. Or if by rituals they just mean that Enchantments similar to Alchemy can't be made on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T03:54:12-07:00","id":1489405,"title":"","content":"\u200bI really hope that Alchemy, Enchantment, and Summoning, Binding, Warding aren't Rituals only in the sense that you have to buy each individual effect you can do with them. Because that means buying up levels in those paths are just paying xp to then pay xp...which is a design philosophy I am not particularly fond of. Like I get that they can't be done on the fly, but I think that is enough of a limiter without having to pour tonnes of xp into each and every recipe and creation one wants to have available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T07:51:24-07:00","id":1489412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489405#post1489405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI really hope that Alchemy, Enchantment, and Summoning, Binding, Warding aren't Rituals only in the sense that you have to buy each individual effect you can do with them. Because that means buying up levels in those paths are just paying xp to then pay xp...which is a design philosophy I am not particularly fond of. Like I get that they can't be done on the fly, but I think that is enough of a limiter without having to pour tonnes of xp into each and every recipe and creation one wants to have available.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I played it with Revised is that Rituals that are simply a Path power performed as a Ritual need not be purchased. If it's simply a way for the sorcerer to trade casting time for the extra successes, I don't see the need to charge XP for that. If it's a specific effect as an expression of the Path that is not covered by Aspects, that's a different thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T09:00:07-07:00","id":1489416,"title":"","content":"Note also that Alchemy and Enchantment explicitly take <i>days</i> rather than <i>turns</i> to work. That's appropriate, given what they do; but it raises questions about how the Ritual rules work with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T09:09:32-07:00","id":1489418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489416#post1489416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note also that Alchemy and Enchantment explicitly take <i>days</i> rather than <i>turns</i> to work. That's appropriate, given what they do; but it raises questions about how the Ritual rules work with them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup that is why I am curious if they meant ritual with a big R(as in the ones you buy with xp) or a small r as in just not being able to do stuff on the fly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T10:11:32-07:00","id":1489489,"title":"","content":"I hope that one thing is addressed in the errata and that is some of the spell scaling...Distance, Passengers, and Travel Speed springs to mind. Because with for example Conveyance if I have it at level 1 as a technomancer who focuses on enhanced versions of traditional vehicles like cars...that path would not be useful to me at all until I get up to like level 4-5. At level 1 I would be able to drive my enhanced car at the same speed as someone jogging...for up to 6 feet or so and to make it work I would have to empty the car of stuff and have no clothes on. This does not seem particularly useful. Hell 100 feet is not exactly vast as far as travel goes, so the path is mostly as useful as jogging and a true master of Conveyance can carry...fewer people than one can stick in an average car.or rubber dingy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T10:22:31-07:00","id":1489492,"title":"","content":"Submit errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T10:37:07-07:00","id":1489494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489492#post1489492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Submit errata.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did and have done that several other times for this one(as in the book not this specific issue)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T11:53:55-07:00","id":1489658,"title":"","content":"I've read it. It doesn't appear to address the core problem I've had with S:REV: The frustrating difficulty/aspect interactions.<br /> <br /> They've actually made it Worse now as the first success doesn't give you the first level in each aspect anymore, you now need those individually And an extra success. Additionally, you need to declare your target number of successes and the spell fails if you don't reach them, as opposed to the player rolling for successes and dishing them out to aspects on the fly.<br /> <br /> They also left in the &quot;round per dot&quot; casting, which no ST in their right mind uses if they want their players using anything other than mundane tools &amp; guns.<br /> <br /> So, pretty unimpressed honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 08-10-2022, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T12:22:20-07:00","id":1489661,"title":"","content":"Errata had been submitted to address some of this; let's see how the final product turns out. But yeah; after meeting it marinate for a bit, I'm less than thrilled with M20 Sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T12:25:58-07:00","id":1489662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489658#post1489658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also left in the &quot;round per dot&quot; casting, which no ST in their right mind uses if they want their players using anything other than mundane tools &amp; guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've ignored this rule for so long, it didn't even register it was still in S20. Having to pay in Willpower for spells already avoids spell spam good enough, imo, while still allowing bursts if needed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T05:37:00-07:00","id":1489737,"title":"","content":"I am literally just hearing about this! I am surprised this got past me since I have been waiting for it to be released. I am going to read through it now and give my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T09:15:24-07:00","id":1489747,"title":"","content":"I like the core of the book, but I agree that the spell casting and ritual mechanics make casting difficult and far too time-consuming. No one wants to spend 3 or 4 rounds trying to cast a spell and 3 days to make a potion or artifact unless it is meant to be a slow-paced game with a lot of downtime. And the number of successes required to cast a spell is pretty prohibitive if you want sorcerer players to do anything magical at all in a short amount of time.<br /> <br /> The ability to hang spells and fast-cast can compensate for this, but those are also pretty expensive to use as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 08-11-2022, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T10:09:35-07:00","id":1489752,"title":"","content":"I submitted errata concerning Hanging spells (They should remove the quintessence cost and clarify that rituals can be hung as well), and allowing Divination to be used with rituals just no specific ones can be taken by default like with other paths. Otherwise, sorcerers of the Cult of Mercury (or with the Ritual Sleeper Flaw) cannot use Divination despite it being one of their favored paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T14:10:44-07:00","id":1489787,"title":"","content":"Hey folks! I'm Travis, the M20 Sorcerer developer. Sorry I'm just now getting over here, but I wanted to thank you all for the discussion, sharing your impressions, and especially for submitting errata. It helps <i><b>immensely</b></i>. A couple things popped up throughout the conversation, which I do want to address just for accuracy:<ul><li>The list of Backgrounds available to Sorcerers is on p. 104. Certain affiliations open up some additional backgrounds as well, noted in the section.</li> <li>The Simplified Aspects rule (p. 14) is meant to offset the difficulty of achieving your Path's potential. <i><b>This is also the rule I personally prefer and use.</b></i></li> <li>Yes, shapeshifting is supposed to be that difficult. <i>Turning a person into a chihuahua without breaking the rules of existence ain't easy</i>. Yes, it's easier to give yourself cat's eyes or ears with illusion than Shapeshifting. It's very much intentional to the design.</li> </ul><br /> I also think there's space for a lot of fun to be had in a campaign where starting sorcerers use full aspects, then as they improved they shift to the Simplified Aspects rule. We are doing this on the actual play I'm running and I'm excited to see how they take the shift next session (though only one spell was cast in session one)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T14:54:43-07:00","id":1489791,"title":"","content":"Quick clarification: \u201cSimplified Aspects\u201d means that the first success that you roll gives you your rating worth of levels in one Aspect, right? <br /> <br /> I still think you need to give a minimum of one level in <i>every</i> Aspect upon <i>any</i> degree of success; because as written, if <i>even one</i> Aspect is at level zero, the spell does nothing. (This is also in keeping with the way SRev did it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T14:58:05-07:00","id":1489792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489791#post1489791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick clarification: \u201cSimplified Aspects\u201d means that the first success that you roll gives you your rating worth of levels in one Aspect, right?<br /> <br /> I still think you need to give a minimum of one level in <i>every</i> Aspect upon <i>any</i> degree of success; because as written, if <i>even one</i> Aspect is at level zero, the spell does nothing. (This is also in keeping with the way SRev did it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay I think I see where we need to clarify.<br /> If you don't buy an aspect in a spell, the spell doesn't have any effects in <i>that aspect</i>. If you need to heal yourself, as an example, you don't need to buy range.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:06:33-07:00","id":1489795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489792#post1489792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, okay I think I see where we need to clarify.<br /> If you don't buy an aspect in a spell, the spell doesn't have any effects in <i>that aspect</i>. If you need to heal yourself, as an example, you don't need to buy range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I thought that that was the intent. The problem is that the text specifically says that if you don't put a success into a given aspect, that aspect is at the \u201cno effect\u201d level, not the \u201cminimum effect\u201d level. I submitted errata on this, using Conjuration as an example: as written, if you don't get four successes (one for the effect, and one for each of the Aspects), you don't get to select even one object to conjure; you don't even get the minimum \u201cless than an ounce\u201d weight for that subject; and you don't even get the \u201cwithin a few feet\u201d distance for the Conjuration. Miss <i>any</i> of those \u2014 again, <i>as written</i> \u2014 and nothing happens.<br /> <br /> Something that you just brought up which wasn't clear from the text is that I didn't get the impression that you could take aspects other than the ones mentioned for a given Path. That is, it didn't look like there was a way to apply range to Healing at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-11-2022, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:12:17-07:00","id":1489796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489795#post1489795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I submitted errata on this, using Conjuration as an example: as written, if you don't get four successes (one for the effect, and one for each of the Aspects), you don't get to select even one object to conjure; you don't even get the minimum \u201cless than an ounce\u201d weight for that subject; and you don't even get the \u201cwithin a few feet\u201d distance for the Conjuration. Miss <i>any</i> of those \u2014 again, <i>as written</i> \u2014 and nothing happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I may not have connected Path-specific errata to that larger issue unless I saw a huge pattern throughout. I think adding a clarifying sentence or two in the Path Magic Core section on Aspects \u2014 that you only need to buy those the spell needs to function \u2014 oughtta do the trick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:19:06-07:00","id":1489797,"title":"","content":"I think what's needed is to treat the way the aspects listed for each path are handled differently from any additional aspects that might be added on on top of them. You should get at least one level in each of the required aspect from the single success needed to make the spell work at all; and I might even go with having all of them operate at your rank in the path from that one success. The optional aspects would start at zero, and I would have no problem buying those up at one level per success.<br /> <br /> That is: the first success on a conjuration roll would give you your rank in conservation as levels in all three of number of targets, weight, and distance; if you choose any additional aspects, those would start at zero and would have to be bought up one level at a time with additional successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-11-2022, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:45:44-07:00","id":1489800,"title":"","content":"Hi Travis, thanks for stopping by! Is it ok to mention things here, or would you prefer them as submitted errata?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489787#post1489787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The list of Backgrounds available to Sorcerers is on p. 104. Certain affiliations open up some additional backgrounds as well, noted in the section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to confirm, Sorcerers not having access to a Quintessence rating via Background purchases (ie the Revised Mana Background) is intended?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489787#post1489787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Simplified Aspects rule (p. 14) is meant to offset the difficulty of achieving your Path's potential. <i><b>This is also the rule I personally prefer and use.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Paths with more aspects to them are a lot harder to cast than Paths with less. For example: Fascination has five aspects, meaning I need to roll at least six successes to cast it, simplified aspect system or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489787#post1489787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, shapeshifting is supposed to be that difficult. <i>Turning a person into a chihuahua without breaking the rules of existence ain't easy</i>. Yes, it's easier to give yourself cat's eyes or ears with illusion than Shapeshifting. It's very much intentional to the design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the intended rule here is &quot;if you want to shift somebody else or make unrelated shifts, you need four extra successes&quot; (or one extra with Path level 4 and the simplified aspects rule), right? If so, I was confused by<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The magician can only affect themselves<br /> and<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Only a single animal feature<br /> <br /> Edit: Ok, it typed too slowly, the aspect questions have already been answered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-11-2022, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:47:35-07:00","id":1489801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489797#post1489797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what's needed is to treat the way the aspects listed for each path are handled differently from any additional aspects that might be added on on top of them. You should get at least one level in each of the required aspect from the single success needed to make the spell work at all; and I might even go with having all of them operate at your rank in the path from that one success. The optional aspects would start at zero, and I would have no problem buying those up at one level per success.<br /> <br /> That is: the first success on a conjuration roll would give you your rank in conservation as levels in all three of number of targets, weight, and distance; if you choose any additional aspects, those would start at zero and would have to be bought up one level at a time with additional successes.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A mixture of the Simplified Aspects and Default Aspects rules sounds fine to me. Since you can add any aspect to a path besides what is typical, you could start out using the default system and then when you say get 3 dots in a path, you use the simplified system and need only 1 success per your dot value in the path. But, like Dataweaver suggested, you still need to get additional success for each additional aspect outside of the default for the path. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T15:56:33-07:00","id":1489802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489787#post1489787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The list of Backgrounds available to Sorcerers is on p. 104. Certain affiliations open up some additional backgrounds as well, noted in the section.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Sorcerers should have access to a sanctum or sanctuary even if they are members of a sorcerer affliation. They have had access to the background since the first edition of sorcerer and many affliations, like the Arcanum, Ancient Order of the Aeon Rites, and Star Council would have sanctums/laboratories sorcerers could use for research and spell casting. If the resources background is meant to represent that, then I think they would miss out on the useful bonuses to rituals and spellcasting from being in such a place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 08-11-2022, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T16:57:47-07:00","id":1489811,"title":"","content":"I haven't had a chance to check since Travis posted that; but if page 104 doesn't address it, my earlier comment about the Avatar background stands: with sorcerer's now using quintessence instead of mana, there's nothing functionally different between a Mana background and the Avatar background, other than \u201cit's Sleeping, and won't be doing anything for you beyond storing Quintessence\u201d. Frankly, I can't think of any Mage Backgrounds that a sorcerer shouldn't have access to. There are a few, like Avatar and Wonders, that warrant some tweaking for sorcerers; but nothing that flat out doesn't work for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T20:34:30-07:00","id":1489829,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the questions! Please always submit to errata, even if you talk to one of us here. We only work off the errata sheets as keeping track of forum posts and the like leads to things being missed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489800#post1489800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Travis, thanks for stopping by! Is it ok to mention things here, or would you prefer them as submitted errata?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just to confirm, Sorcerers not having access to a Quintessence rating via Background purchases (ie the Revised Mana Background) is intended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Outside of Quintessence Manipulation, the only access Sorcerers have to Quintessence is via Tass, and then only if the Resonance is appropriate (if you're using Resonance rules anyway)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T20:37:07-07:00","id":1489830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489811#post1489811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't had a chance to check since Travis posted that; but if page 104 doesn't address it, my earlier comment about the Avatar background stands: with sorcerer's now using quintessence instead of mana, there's nothing functionally different between a Mana background and the Avatar background, other than \u201cit's Sleeping, and won't be doing anything for you beyond storing Quintessence\u201d. Frankly, I can't think of any Mage Backgrounds that a sorcerer shouldn't have access to. There are a few, like Avatar and Wonders, that warrant some tweaking for sorcerers; but nothing that flat out doesn't work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> pg.104 states &quot;Characters aligned with the Disparate Alliance or the Traditions may include Chantry, Node, Retainers, and Sanctum in their available Background choices.&quot; I will suggest an errata to allow these for Sorcerers except Node (would require high levels in Quintessence Manipulation) and Chantry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T20:38:21-07:00","id":1489831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starcomet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489801#post1489801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> But, like Dataweaver suggested, you still need to get additional success for each additional aspect outside of the default for the path. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to purchase any aspects that don't occur with the spell. For example, with Fascination, you don't need to buy Allure and Willbending. You can buy one or the other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T20:42:13-07:00","id":1489832,"title":"","content":"Sanctum is disallowed outside Ascension War factions because it requires Awakened power to make one. You basically need to be able to Terranorm the area or more likely jolt it with Prime Magick (among other things) It's beyond the reach of the hedge wizard to fundamentally alter reality, which a Sanctum requires.<br /> As far as the Avatar goes, it's pretty straightforward: they aren't awakened, so no Avatar Rating.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T21:30:16-07:00","id":1489834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489831#post1489831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to purchase any aspects that don't occur with the spell. For example, with Fascination, you don't need to buy Allure and Willbending. You can buy one or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how the system came across to me:<br /> <br /> With Fascination, you need Number of Targets, Range, Sympathetic Connection, Allure, and Willbending. As I read it, those five are the Aspects that occur with the spell, and thus are the ones you need to spend successes on. The ones that <i>don't</i> occur with the spell are Area, Damage/Healing, Distance, Duration, Metaphysical Weight, Passengers, Travel Speed, and Weight. Of <i>course</i> those are zero; what puzzles me is why it would make sense to spend successes on any of them. <br /> <br /> As well: the requirement that the ones that you spend successes on (the first five) all start out at zero: not <i>even</i> a single target (Number of Targets \u2022); not <i>even</i> Touch Only (Range \u2022); not <i>even</i> Direct Physical Contact (Sympathetic Connection \u2022); not <i>even</i> one die to add to social dice pools (Allure \u2022); not <i>even</i> Intriguing (Willbending \u2022). <br /> <br /> By my understanding, you would need six successes to achieve a <i>minimal</i> result; anything less than that, and at least one crucial Aspect is left at \u201cbelow minimum\u201d status, and the entire Effect is undermined. <br /> <br /> Again, that's my understanding of what the rules say. What was the actual <i>intent</i>? If possible, I'd like a description of a worked example of casting a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-12-2022, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T21:46:20-07:00","id":1489835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489829#post1489829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the questions! Please always submit to errata, even if you talk to one of us here. We only work off the errata sheets as keeping track of forum posts and the like leads to things being missed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Correct. Outside of Quintessence Manipulation, the only access Sorcerers have to Quintessence is via Tass, and then only if the Resonance is appropriate (if you're using Resonance rules anyway)</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that this undermines The Flow of Ki, Force of Spirit, and Strength of Psyche: all three of these Merits involve spending Quintessence from the sorcerer's internal reserves, and carry the disclaimer that the sorcerer must be able to store Quintessence in their own pattern to be eligible for the Merit. Since you're saying that sorcerers can never store Quintessence in their own pattern, these three Merits are utterly useless to sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T23:13:26-07:00","id":1489838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489795#post1489795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that you just brought up which wasn't clear from the text is that I didn't get the impression that you could take aspects other than the ones mentioned for a given Path. That is, it didn't look like there was a way to apply range to Healing at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't imagine this to be the case; it would mean you could use Sympathetic Connection on something like Hellfire and with some effort set people on fire remotely from the safety of your Ritual space.<br /> I do like Range on Healing though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T00:59:45-07:00","id":1489854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489829#post1489829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the questions! Please always submit to errata, even if you talk to one of us here. We only work off the errata sheets as keeping track of forum posts and the like leads to things being missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a deadline for submissions? I have two Sorcerers in my running campaign and would like to ask them if they would be willing to test-drive the S20 rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489835#post1489835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that this undermines The Flow of Ki, Force of Spirit, and Strength of Psyche: all three of these Merits involve spending Quintessence from the sorcerer's internal reserves, and carry the disclaimer that the sorcerer must be able to store Quintessence in their own pattern to be eligible for the Merit. Since you're saying that sorcerers can never store Quintessence in their own pattern, these three Merits are utterly useless to sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I read it correctly, storing Quintessence is a Flow \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 function (p.44).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T04:33:57-07:00","id":1489872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489832#post1489832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanctum is disallowed outside Ascension War factions because it requires Awakened power to make one. You basically need to be able to Terranorm the area or more likely jolt it with Prime Magick (among other things) It's beyond the reach of the hedge wizard to fundamentally alter reality, which a Sanctum requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then make a unique sorcerer only background called Sanctuary as in the original WOD:Sorcerer. It is basically a specially prepared sacred space that contains all of the necessary materials needed for your rituals, alchemy, enchantments, and provides extra dice/difficulty break on spellcasting or ritual casting. It also has low level Arcane/Cloak. If not, I will likely just house rule that the Sanctuary from WOD:Sorcerer can be used by my sorcerer players and suggest that to other STs I play with as a sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 08-12-2022, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T05:35:59-07:00","id":1489876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489832#post1489832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanctum is disallowed outside Ascension War factions because it requires Awakened power to make one. You basically need to be able to Terranorm the area or more likely jolt it with Prime Magick (among other things) It's beyond the reach of the hedge wizard to fundamentally alter reality, which a Sanctum requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That whole 'disallowed outside of factions' sounds like a personal view or house rule, not a point from the M20 book.<br /> <br /> 'Regardless of its nature, this space must be specially<br /> prepared by the group or mage who uses it, with constant<br /> maintenance (no less than once per month) to keep the space<br /> attuned to the people who use it.' - M20 p324<br /> <br /> None of the above implies that creating and maintaining a Sanctum is equivalent to the effort required to create a Node<br /> <br /> 'A Sanctum can range from a small herb-garden with wards<br /> set against intruders and trees planted to screen the place off from<br /> casual viewing to small laboratories filled with gleaming scientific<br /> gear. Martial-arts studios, yoga lofts, sacred groves, basement dens,<br /> band practice spaces, penthouse suites, photography studios,<br /> tiny shrines on remote mountaintops \u2013 the Sanctum or Lab is<br /> whatever you want it to be' - M20 p324<br /> <br /> Since Sanctum is a Background available to any character, even an Arete 1 Mage student, and reading the above its fairly clear that Sanctums can also occur or be created through other means other than a 'big wizard' creating them. So no, Sanctums are not 'out of the reach' of hedge wizards. It is however a campaign balance decision as to wether or not Sanctum is available to Sorcerers, although personally I can't see any reason to restrict it other than anti-sorcerer bias.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wrongfun Issue<br /> <br /> To add to this area, I've noticed that one problem with WoD products in general is that there is a definite bias against Sorcerers and other second class choices like Ghouls, etc. and this attitude also comes across on various forums.<br /> <br /> To me that seems like its a wrongfun problem - i.e. you should play a Vampire, playing a Ghoul is wrongfun so you have to be penalised, or you should play a Mage, playing a Sorcerer is wrongfun so they have to be weaker, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> So for me playing a Sorcerer or a Psychic in Mage (or a Ghoul in Vampire, or Kinfolk in Werewolf) should not require you to play as a second class character and thus the rules should be improved so that those choices are balanced, even if the original authors haven't thought it through properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 08-12-2022, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T05:43:16-07:00","id":1489877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489835#post1489835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that this undermines The Flow of Ki, Force of Spirit, and Strength of Psyche: all three of these Merits involve spending Quintessence from the sorcerer's internal reserves, and carry the disclaimer that the sorcerer must be able to store Quintessence in their own pattern to be eligible for the Merit. Since you're saying that sorcerers can never store Quintessence in their own pattern, these three Merits are utterly useless to sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers can store Quintessence through Quintessence Manipulation<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T05:45:32-07:00","id":1489878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489838#post1489838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't imagine this to be the case; it would mean you could use Sympathetic Connection on something like Hellfire and with some effort set people on fire remotely from the safety of your Ritual space.<br /> I do like Range on Healing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can absolutely use a sympathetic connection with Hellfire to light someone aflame from your Ritual Space. Now you're thinking like a Sorcerer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T05:48:02-07:00","id":1489879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489854#post1489854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a deadline for submissions? I have two Sorcerers in my running campaign and would like to ask them if they would be willing to test-drive the S20 rules.<br /> <br /> If I read it correctly, storing Quintessence is a Flow \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 function (p.44).</div> </div> </div> </div>Errata is unfortunately ending pretty soon. I would imagine in the next week, though I can't say for sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T05:53:20-07:00","id":1489880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489876#post1489876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That whole 'disallowed outside of factions' sounds like a personal view or house rule, not a point from the M20 book.<br /> <br /> 'Regardless of its nature, this space must be specially<br /> prepared by the group or mage who uses it, with constant<br /> maintenance (no less than once per month) to keep the space<br /> attuned to the people who use it.' - M20 p324<br /> <br /> None of the above implies that creating and maintaining a Sanctum is equivalent to the effort required to create a Node<br /> <br /> 'A Sanctum can range from a small herb-garden with wards<br /> set against intruders and trees planted to screen the place off from<br /> casual viewing to small laboratories filled with gleaming scientific<br /> gear. Martial-arts studios, yoga lofts, sacred groves, basement dens,<br /> band practice spaces, penthouse suites, photography studios,<br /> tiny shrines on remote mountaintops \u2013 the Sanctum or Lab is<br /> whatever you want it to be' - M20 p324<br /> <br /> Since Sanctum is a Background available to any character, even an Arete 1 Mage student, and reading the above its fairly clear that Sanctums can also occur or be created through other means other than a 'big wizard' creating them. So no, Sanctums are not 'out of the reach' of hedge wizards. It is however a campaign balance decision as to wether or not Sanctum is available to Sorcerers, although personally I can't see any reason to restrict it other than anti-sorcerer bias.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wrongfun Issue<br /> <br /> To add to this area, I've noticed that one problem with WoD products in general is that there is a definite bias against Sorcerers and other second class choices like Ghouls, etc. and this attitude also comes across on various forums.<br /> <br /> To me that seems like its a wrongfun problem - i.e. you should play a Vampire, playing a Ghoul is wrongfun so you have to be penalised, or you should play a Mage, playing a Sorcerer is wrongfun so they have to be weaker, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> So for me playing a Sorcerer or a Psychic in Mage (or a Ghoul in Vampire, or Kinfolk in Werewolf) should not require you to play as a second class character and thus the rules should be improved so that those choices are balanced, even if the original authors haven't thought it through properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm merely explaining the design intent of the rules. Your reasoning makes sense, so use it at your table, however I didn't say it takes the same effort required to make a Node to make a Sanctum. I said it was closer to a Terranorming effort, albeit on a limited scale.<br /> <br /> I want people to play Sorcerers and have fun. I've loved Sorcerer since 1st edition and wanted to design something for them since 1997. I assure you, I'm not applying any anti-sorcerer bias. Sorcerers are weaker than Mages in some respects and stronger in others and that's what makes them different, wonderful, and cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T06:07:03-07:00","id":1489881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489878#post1489878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can absolutely use a sympathetic connection with Hellfire to light someone aflame from your Ritual Space. Now you're thinking like a Sorcerer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's nice and opens up a whole lot of creative options. It should be made explicit in the rules though, and maybe requires some clarification on how Area effects are handled- split dice pool among targets in the area?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489879#post1489879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errata is unfortunately ending pretty soon. I would imagine in the next week, though I can't say for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I need to fast forward a bit in this case. I think I at least want to convert the characters from Rev to S20 as a test to see if I notice any problems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:05:25-07:00","id":1489917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489881#post1489881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh that's nice and opens up a whole lot of creative options. It should be made explicit in the rules though, and maybe requires some clarification on how Area effects are handled- split dice pool among targets in the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>Area causes the effect to be applied to everything in the area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489881#post1489881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I need to fast forward a bit in this case. I think I at least want to convert the characters from Rev to S20 as a test to see if I notice any problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to your feedback.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:29:33-07:00","id":1489921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489917#post1489917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look forward to your feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm done, conversion is overall very easy and frictionless, so I will only mention the points I noticed.<br /> I updated two characters, a Medium and an Oneiromancer.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes, Abilities, Affiliation:</b><br /> - No favored Attributes are given for affiliations with Traditions, Crafts, and Conventions. Not a big deal, it's easy to check M20 and extrapolate.<br /> - Same for favored Paths for most of them, although the Crafts have lists. Again, no big deal.<br /> - No specialized Abilities for Sorcerers in S20. M20's list of Secondary Abilities is extensive, but some dedicated Abilities that complement Paths would have been nice. Notably, my Medium player would miss out on Normalcy and Spiritual Awareness.<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b><br /> - Both of the characters have the Mana Background, which has been dropped. This would be a hard sell to my players, and I will keep it as a house rule with Quintessence.<br /> - My Medium happens to be Bata'a affiliated, and would lose the Chol\u00e9 Background. As with specialized Abilities, a few more specialized Backgrounds instead of fewer would have been nice. Again, house ruling this in.<br /> - Sanctuary has already been mentioned, but the Oneiromancer would also lose their Demesne. As there is even a specific Ritual for invading a Demesne, I will submit this as erratum. I see really no reason why a Sorcerer could not have a Demesne.<br /> <br /> <b>Paths:</b><br /> - The Medium is using Ephemera from WtO: The Quick &amp; the Dead, as it was absent from Sorcerer Revised. It's nice to have it back, and it's a good fit. Ephemera has no associated sample Rituals listed in S20, while WtO:Q&amp;D provides a few useful examples of 'friendly' necromantic Rituals. Might be worth a look for adaption, as well as Rites from W20 for interaction with spirits.<br /> - Mortal Necromancy is a welcome addition and will likely replace the homebrew we used instead.<br /> - As a note, the Oneiromancer also has a few dots in Enchantment and Mana (Quintessence) Manipulation, which they used together to great effect. It might be worth writing a sentence or two on synergetic effects, especially for Rituals using more than one Path.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:35:17-07:00","id":1489922,"title":"","content":"A minor nitpick: I can understand the etymology behind calling it mortal necromancy; however, I would not expect Sorcerers to call it that. To them, it would just be necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:48:42-07:00","id":1489925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489921#post1489921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm done, conversion is overall very easy and frictionless, so I will only mention the points I noticed.<br /> I updated two characters, a Medium and an Oneiromancer.<br /> <br /> - Sanctuary has already been mentioned, but the Oneiromancer would also lose their Demesne. As there is even a specific Ritual for invading a Demesne, I will submit this as erratum. I see really no reason why a Sorcerer could not have a Demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely agree. Demense should be available.Thanks for submitting!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:05:05-07:00","id":1489931,"title":"","content":"Could you maybe fold Artifact into Wonder, and use the space saved to explain which made backgrounds don't make the cut, and why not? Or at the very least, add a \u201csee p.XX for a list of the permissible Backgrounds\u201d reference to the end of the first paragraph under backgrounds? I will be submitting errata to that effect shortly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T04:32:31-07:00","id":1490012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489931#post1489931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you maybe fold Artifact into Wonder, and use the space saved to explain which made backgrounds don't make the cut, and why not? Or at the very least, add a \u201csee p.XX for a list of the permissible Backgrounds\u201d reference to the end of the first paragraph under backgrounds? I will be submitting errata to that effect shortly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifact is systematically different from Wonder, which is why it's there. It specifically reflects items created through sorcery/hedge magic. However a p. XX to point folks to the Character Creation section for the BG list is absolutely doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T06:19:17-07:00","id":1490019,"title":"","content":"While Mana Manipulation was an optional path in revised for gameplay purposes, it is now clear Quintessence Manipulation is a high priority path that at least one sorcerer player in a cabal should pick. <br /> <br /> It is important for not only lowering difficulties but also to hang spells/rituals if my errata suggestion is not taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T08:24:47-07:00","id":1490029,"title":"","content":"The biggest <i>mechanical </i>problem with QM I see at the moment is that the ability to store Quintessence is locked behind Path level 4, meaning anyone who wants to make use of one of the Merits <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> mentioned has to at least unlock this level on character creation to actually use the Merits from the start. It also functionally makes the Merits specialized powers of the QM Path, even though they seem to be intended for use in different character archetypes.<br /> <br /> Edit 1:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489917#post1489917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Area causes the effect to be applied to everything in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to bring this up again, but why would a Sorcerer use the Passengers Aspect for Conveyance when they could get far better results with Area? Can I mass bind spirits in the same area?<br /> <br /> I understand and like the intent of generally applicable aspects, but I'm afraid it breaks a few things without stricter regulation. (Of course, the ST can call foul but we all know rules lawyers)<br /> <br /> Edit 2:<br /> The more I think about it, the more I hope there is going to be some clarifications. Think about Paths that usually don't use Aspects- Enchanting or Alchemically altering a place, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-13-2022, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T09:54:30-07:00","id":1490037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Broskandar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1489003#post1489003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I imagined they wouldn't put the 6th-Dot powers in Sorcerer20, which is a shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>6 dot powers in S20? Really?<br /> <br /> Based.<br /> <br /> I'm getting this now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T12:08:25-07:00","id":1490045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1490037#post1490037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 6 dot powers in S20? Really?<br /> <br /> Based.<br /> <br /> I'm getting this now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book states &quot;Going beyond the fifth dot in an Aspect may be possible but is the stuff of legend most magicians never see, much less accomplish.&quot; (pg.13) So it is essentially up to the ST and players to decide whether they want to include the 6th dot in their chronicle. I assume it would become essentially equivalent to narrative spells and rituals that are of legendary quality. Alchemy 6 being able to make the philosopher stone, immortality, and acheving awakening, Fascination 6 able to charm a town or a small city full of people, S/B/W 6 able to affect gods, devils, etc, Fortune 6 able to casting a bless or curse that can last for several generations and affect an entire city or organization and their decendents are all examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T10:27:45-07:00","id":1490147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1490029#post1490029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest <i>mechanical </i>problem with QM I see at the moment is that the ability to store Quintessence is locked behind Path level 4, meaning anyone who wants to make use of one of the Merits <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> mentioned has to at least unlock this level on character creation to actually use the Merits from the start. It also functionally makes the Merits specialized powers of the QM Path, even though they seem to be intended for use in different character archetypes.<br /> <br /> Edit 1:<br /> <br /> Sorry to bring this up again, but why would a Sorcerer use the Passengers Aspect for Conveyance when they could get far better results with Area? Can I mass bind spirits in the same area?<br /> <br /> I understand and like the intent of generally applicable aspects, but I'm afraid it breaks a few things without stricter regulation. (Of course, the ST can call foul but we all know rules lawyers)<br /> <br /> Edit 2:<br /> The more I think about it, the more I hope there is going to be some clarifications. Think about Paths that usually don't use Aspects- Enchanting or Alchemically altering a place, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wherever we can apply clarifications in errata, we will. Conveyance typically uses Passengers, not Area, but if that needs to be clarified in the text we can do that.<br /> <br /> Editing to add: On second thought <i>you could use Area </i>instead of Passengers, however you would bring everything in the area with you. Friends, foes, and inanimate objects.<br /> <br /> I don't expect any ground-level overhauls (reworking an entire Path, moving all the path specific aspects into the general aspects section of the book, adding the 6-th dot of anything) to occur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"TravisLegge","date":"above, silly. 08-14-2022, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T10:47:15-07:00","id":1490148,"title":"","content":"That was actually the main motive behind my suggestion concerning the Avatar Background (which I <i>do</i> think fits, because even Sleepers have Avatars; it's just that for most people, there's not much that a Sleeping Avatar can <i>do</i>): you could have all of the benefits of the SRev Mana Background packed into a sentence or two of text. (e.g., \u201cSorcerers can take dots in Avatar; but since the Avatar is Sleeping, the only benefit this provides is the ability to store Quintessence in your Pattern.\u201d)<br /> <br /> But I won't push the matter further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-14-2022, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T10:53:26-07:00","id":1490152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1490147#post1490147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wherever we can apply clarifications in errata, we will. Conveyance uses Passengers, not Area, but if that needs to be clarified in the text we can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you, talking about some specifics here already helped a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1490147#post1490147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect any ground-level overhauls (reworking an entire Path, moving all the path specific aspects into the general aspects section of the book, adding the 6-th dot of anything) to occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that there are limits to what can still be done with errata. As a suggestion, a brief list of optional Aspects for each Path might do the trick.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T17:33:43-07:00","id":1490660,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to pop in and offer my thanks to everyone who turned in errata for M20 Sorcerer. Your feedback has been invaluable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T16:26:24-07:00","id":1490820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1490660#post1490660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to pop in and offer my thanks to everyone who turned in errata for M20 Sorcerer. Your feedback has been invaluable.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'd like to thank you for being so approachable and open about this. I've got no stake in the book, but I really enjoyed seeing the participants discuss it and your engagement with them. So thanks to you and to everyone looking to make Sorceror even better!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T04:56:18-07:00","id":1490866,"title":"","content":"Yeah, thanks for the community engagement! I appreciate the dialogue a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T18:13:01-07:00","id":1490959,"title":"","content":"Happy to. Thank you both!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:15:54-07:00","id":1510380,"title":"","content":"So where is the errata?<br /> <br /> Nevermind, found it after I posted.<br /> <br /> Still find it annoying that shapeshifting is impossible until you have 3 dots in it and it requires 7 successes for the simplest of things. Three dots of shapeshifting to change your eye color. Outrageous.<br /> <br /> And why is it the better you are at a path, the harder it is to do that path? Again, Shapeshifting. You just want to change your eye color. Why is the difficulty now 9 because you have the path at a 5, when at one point the difficulty was a 5 when you had it at a 1 (sure it would be 7 because you need 3 dots just to cast the thing on yourself.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","user":"Thkaal","date":". 05-01-2023, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T11:31:43-07:00","id":1510383,"title":"","content":"The difficulty isn't based on the number of dots you <i>have; </i>it's based on the number of dots you <i>need. </i>A casting that becomes available at the first rank is difficulty 5 whether you have one dot or five dots in the Path; but if the casting only becomes available when you get the fifth dot, it will be difficulty 9 once you're able to cast it.<br /> <br /> You're right: Shapeshifting is screwed up. Every Aspect in the book ought to have a \u201czero level\u201d that defines how the spell works if you don't put any successes into that Aspect; or the first success in the spell should give you one success in every Aspect, with the Aspects all starting at one dot. But having \u201caffects yourself\u201d and \u201conly a single animal\u201d as <i>level 3 Aspects? </i>Nope; that simply doesn't work. Whoever decided to bump those up from 1 to 3 messed up, big time. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-01-2023, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T13:18:30-07:00","id":1510397,"title":"","content":"Oddly, that's what I thought at first, but if you take a literal interpretation instead of what makes sense....<br /> <br /> I'm using Scale as what you can do.<br /> <br /> Subject is<br /> x Self (Because.....well...that just makes sense that you have to affect something)<br /> ** Someone else<br /> **** Two people +* per additional person.<br /> <br /> Disparity<br /> ** An animal aspect.<br /> **** Two different animals' aspects +* per additional animal's aspect<br /> <br /> Scale determines difficulty, need a minimum of 1 dot just to manipulate the magic. So the slightest change is 1 success (like having green instead of brown eyes). But giving yourself gills requires 3. Even turning into a fish is 3 successes, if it's a single kind of fish you're turning into as opposed to borrowing different fish parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T13:54:22-07:00","id":1510404,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I just use <b>Sorcery: Paths of Power</b>, from Storyteller's Vault. It was written by one of the guys who wrote <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> and was very likely the inspiration for the latter; but it has a major advantage over the one that Onyx Path published: <i>it's not broken.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</i>I say that with regret, because I try not to be negative about Onyx Path products. But I'm not being hyperbolic or stating a personal preference as fact; I'm stating an objective truth. <b>M20 Sorcerer</b>, if played as written, is broken in at least two ways, the big one being the way it handles Aspects. <b>S:PoP</b> <i>isn't</i> broken: for instance, the Shapeshifting Aspects are ranked X to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. Shift Scale goes from \u201cminor cosmetic changes\u201d at X to \u201cmythic animal forms\u201d at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; Subject is \u201cself\u201d at X, \u201cone other person\u201d at \u2022\u2022\u2022, \u201ctwo other people\u201d at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, and \u201cthree other people\u201d at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; and Disparity is \u201cone animal feature\u201d at X, \u201ctwo animals\u201d at \u2022\u2022\u2022, \u201cthree animals\u201d at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, and \u201cany number of animal features\u201d at \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. And that's the pattern throughout: there's <i>always</i> an X for every Aspect, saying what happens if you don't put any successes into it.<br /> <br /> And I'm going to say \u201cI told you so!\u201d Because I <i>did. </i>Or rather, I told <i>them</i> so: during the review phase when they were collecting errata, I submitted a couple of issues pointing out the brokenness of the Aspects as written as well as simple fixes that wouldn't change the wording much.<br /> <br /> I <i>could</i> go through <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> and house rule away the bugs that didn't get addressed when they were supposed to, and it wouldn't even be all that hard to do so. But as I already own <b>Paths of Power</b>, I'm not going to bother. I'll just use <i>that</i> as written. Mostly. (I never use <i>anything</i> precisely as written; but there's a lot less in <b>Paths of Power</b> that I'd change, and none of the changes would be of the \u201cfixing problems\u201d variety: they're all \u201cI like it better this way\u201d.)<b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-09-2023, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:50:02-07:00","id":1510416,"title":"","content":"I had been using PoP for a game I was in. Then I found out M20 Sorcerer existed. Bought it but really didn't read it until this new chronicle I'm starting and....looking over everything about it, it's so much more broken than Mage ever was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T14:50:16-07:00","id":1510417,"title":"","content":"My group has settled on these house fixes:<br /> <br /> - First dot of any aspect that is required to cast a spell is covered by the initial success (= they are x values)<br /> - Sorcerer patterns can store QE without having access to the QE Manipulation path, via background (= the revised Mana background)<br /> - Sanctuary is an allowed background<br /> <br /> That's basically back to Revised rules to some extent. I like the more flexible application of general aspects though.<br /> I'm also rather generous with restoring WP (using the Meditation skill or resting in the Sanctum or Demesne), as they can trickle away pretty quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T15:10:21-07:00","id":1510419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1510404#post1510404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I just use <b>Sorcery: Paths of Power</b>, from Storyteller's Vault. It was written by one of the guys who wrote <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> and was very likely the inspiration for the latter; but it has a major advantage over the one that Onyx Path published: [I]it's not broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> Still deeply annoyed that PoP doubled down on attaching sorcerer to mage and even attached the paths to the sphere system. I've hated the idea of sorcerers as &quot;mage ghouls&quot; and all the unnecessary baggage that comes with that since revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T04:55:46-07:00","id":1511118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1510417#post1510417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also rather generous with restoring WP (using the Meditation skill or resting in the Sanctum or Demesne), as they can trickle away pretty quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is important for sorcerer characters because they need to spend WP for every spell and ritual they cast, and it is easy to quickly run out depending on what you are doing. Making WP hard to recover really hamstrings sorcerer characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:01:10-07:00","id":1511120,"title":"","content":"This is also why I don't like the decision that was made to completely remove the Mana background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:11:04-07:00","id":1511121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1511120#post1511120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also why I don't like the decision that was made to completely remove the Mana background.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the mana background should not have been removed, but there were some fans who felt it complicated things to have another source of energy that was somehow different from quintessence that needed to be tracked. We already have Vitae, Gnosis, Glamour, etc. but that could have been solved by just simply calling it Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:14:51-07:00","id":1511122,"title":"","content":"That's easy enough to address. Just provide a background that provides quintessence the way that the Avatar background does, but without the \u201cyou have a guide\u201d aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:21:52-07:00","id":1511123,"title":"","content":"That makes perfect sense. I understand the authors wanted to make sorcerers more unique by not being able to manipulate quintessence as easy as mages, but this has been a thing since revised and from a lore perspective it makes sense. As it is right now, you need the Quintessence Manipulation Path to make ample use of Quintessence unless your sorcerer is part of a fellowship/group that has stores of tass to hand out. That however does make the ST the final arbiter as to how much quintessence your character is allowed to use.<br /> <br /> I will tell my current ST to remove the need for quintessence to hang spells and rituals as that just makes it even harder to prepare spells before hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 05-09-2023, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:32:37-07:00","id":1511124,"title":"","content":"It also nerfs several of the Merits that the book provides: the ones that let you spend Quintessence to reduce the difficulty of physical, mental, or social tasks. If you don't have relatively easy access to Quintessence, those Merits generally aren't worth the points. <br /> <br /> And this is another example of why I recommend to just go with S:PoP instead of S20, possibly with a handful of minor tweaks like substituting \u201cQuintessence\u201d for \u201cMana\u201d (such as in the Techn\u00e9 background, which is the Mana background renamed). Frankly, the only thing that S20 does that S:PoP doesn't do is to include the Numina from <b>Ghost Hunters</b>; and it does that by sacrificing a number of other Paths that are much more worthy of inclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:41:51-07:00","id":1511125,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I have told my current ST to use S:PoP, Sorcerer's Companion, and S20 to help balance everything out. S20 on its own is adequate but does leaves a few things to be desired.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T05:46:01-07:00","id":1511126,"title":"","content":"I also fear the STs who are purist and anti-ST vault will force players to use S20 only despite its flaws. They would need to house rule many things, but at that point they might as well just use S:PoP and Sorcerer's companion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T20:44:51-07:00","id":1512328,"title":"","content":"I've been skimming through Sorcerer 20 because a player was thinking about playing one (they ended up going for a Mage). Regarding the Aspects, I got the impression that the intent was that a single success gets you everything at the first dot (either from the standard Aspects or the Path-specfic ones), just like regular Mage without using Dividing Successes. Alternatively, you can build it success by success, spending a success per dot that you use, like you would with Dividing Successes, if you prefer that system. Are there any examples in the book that support either of these views?<br /> <br /> Also, with Shapeshifting, it looked like it was trying to mirror the Life Sphere, with transforming others requiring 4 dots and the Scale Aspects echoing that Sphere. It's obviously not as powerful as Life but it seemed to be following the same structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T03:21:33-07:00","id":1512343,"title":"","content":"The problem is that S20 says that if you don't spend any successes on an Aspect, you get that Aspect at zero: \u201cWhen the hedge magician casts a spell, they must choose what level of each Aspect they want to include, with the default being zero \u2014 and therefore no effect \u2014 in each \u2026 When the spell is cast, it requires one success for each rank in each Aspect\u201d (p.13). But then it defines the <i>first </i>dot of the Aspect as something that, in practice, you need in order for the spell to do <i>anything. </i>Shapeshifting is particularly bad because two of its three Aspects, as written, need three successes <i>each</i> in order to do anything. (The text goes on to say that \u201ca result of no effect purchased in one Aspect doesn't impede any other Aspect\u201d; but that's moot if the Aspect is defining something that the spell cannot do without, like how much of a change to make, who it affects, or how much variety you have to choose amongst.<br /> <br /> Illustrating: if you don't put at least one success into Scale, you're not even able to make <i>cosmetic </i>changes; if you can't even do that, then it doesn't matter how many subjects you can affect our how many animals you can borrow features from: zero successes into Scale means that you can't do anything with it. Likewise, if you don't put <i>at least three successes</i> into Subject, you can't even Shapeshift <i>yourself</i>. Again, it doesn't matter how many successes you put into Scale or Disparity; you can't do anything if you can't affect anyone. Likewise with the minimum of three successes for Disparity: without that, you don't even get <i>one </i>animal feature to apply. Subject and Scale don't matter if you don't put the minimum number of successes into Disparity. Thus, as written, you cannot do <i>anything </i>with Shapeshifting until you have put 1+3+3=7 successes into its Aspects. And since you can't put any more successes into an Aspect than you have ranks in the Path, you can't put the three successes into Subject that are needed to affect yourself, or the three successes into Disparity that are needed to select a single animal feature, until you have at least three dots in Shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Broken as written.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not hard to patch. I suspect that the reason you read it the way that you did is because that makes <s>more</s> sense: say that a single success gets you one level in each Aspect that's specifically mentioned in the Path write-up (so Scale, Subject, and Disparity for Shapeshifting, or Duration, Number of Targets, Senses, and Realism for Illusion), with any <i>other</i> Aspects starting at zero <i>if they're allowed at all,</i> and additional successes divided among the Aspects after that. That fixes <i>most</i> of the problems, though you still need to change Shapeshifting's Subject and Disparity Aspects so that they go \u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 instead of \u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; because no mandatory Aspect (by which I mean \u201can Aspect that cripples the spell if you don't put successes into it\u201d) should ever have a requirement of more than one success to do something.<br /> <br /> In short, my problem with the Subject Aspect of Shapeshifting isn't the \u201cfour dots to affect others\u201d; it's the \u201cthree dots to affect <i>yourself</i>\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-22-2023, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T04:40:06-07:00","id":1512346,"title":"","content":"In a somewhat more positive note, I do like how M20 Sorcerer consolidated the common Aspects into one section up front, implying that any of them can be applied to any Path. In theory, this makes Path Magic much more flexible. Unfortunately, they didn't consider the implications. You can't meaningfully apply Area to Shapeshifting, for instance: while it's a logical thing to do, the ability to Shapeshift everyone in an area for one or two successes would completely undermine the fact that you need four successes to Shapeshift someone else, and five successes to Shapeshift two other people. So I wouldn't allow the Area Aspect to be applied to Shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T07:43:32-07:00","id":1512357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1488753-m20-sorcerer-advance-pdf-on-sale-wednesday?p=1512343#post1512343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...though you still need to change Shapeshifting's Subject and Disparity Aspects so that they go \u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 instead of \u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022/\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022; because no mandatory Aspect (by which I mean \u201can Aspect that cripples the spell if you don't put successes into it\u201d) should ever have a requirement of more than one success to do something...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's a really interesting point to note. It's an odd outlier like that. Thanks for your thoughts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}